    the immune globulin is an approved pooled plasma derivative for the treatment of primary immune deficiency disease.
    the immune globulin is administered in the home.
    the finding home administration appropriate about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the order for the immune globulin is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the immune globulin is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the immune globulin includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the immune globulin includes order date.
    the order for the immune globulin includes description of the item.
    the order for the immune globulin includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the immune globulin includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the immune globulin was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the immune globulin was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].
    flip expects changes [["add: the supplier holds proof of delivery for the immune globulin"]].

% Alyglo billed as J1552 in November 2024, before the code took effect, and
% a two-month supply of Privigen: both reasonable and necessary, both fail
% the policy's payment conditions at the remedy.
scenario coding_and_dispensing is:
    claim 1 is for the alyglo.
    the HCPCS code of the alyglo is "J1552".
    the alyglo is furnished to Fay.
    the residence of Fay is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2024-11-01.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the diagnosis code of Fay is "D80.0".
    the alyglo is an approved pooled plasma derivative for the treatment of primary immune deficiency disease.
    the alyglo is administered in the home.
    the finding home administration appropriate about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the order for the alyglo is dated 2024-10-20.
    the order for the alyglo is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the alyglo includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the alyglo includes order date.
    the order for the alyglo includes description of the item.
    the order for the alyglo includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the alyglo includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the alyglo was communicated to the supplier on 2024-10-22.
    the alyglo was delivered on 2024-11-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the alyglo.
    claim 2 is for the immune globulin.
    the HCPCS code of the immune globulin is "J1459".
    the immune globulin is furnished to Fay.
    the date of service of claim 2 is 2024-11-01.
    claim 2 is for a supply of 2 months.
    the immune globulin is an approved pooled plasma derivative for the treatment of primary immune deficiency disease.
    the immune globulin is administered in the home.
    the order for the immune globulin is dated 2024-10-20.
    the order for the immune globulin is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the immune globulin includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the immune globulin includes order date.
    the order for the immune globulin includes description of the item.
    the order for the immune globulin includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the immune globulin includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the immune globulin was communicated to the supplier on 2024-10-22.
    the immune globulin was delivered on 2024-11-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the immune globulin.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].

% Home administration and the finding. Gus: the Council finds it
% unsupported — not reasonable and necessary. Hal: nobody has made the
% finding — the answer is conditional on it.
scenario home_administration_findings is:
    claim 1 is for the immune globulin.
    the HCPCS code of the immune globulin is "J1459".
    the immune globulin is furnished to Gus.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the diagnosis code of Gus is "D80.0".
    the immune globulin is an approved pooled plasma derivative for the treatment of primary immune deficiency disease.
    the immune globulin is administered in the home.
    the finding home administration appropriate about Gus is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the record contains no determination by the treating practitioner that home infusion is appropriate, only the supplier's intake form".
    claim 2 is for the other immune globulin.
    the HCPCS code of the other immune globulin is "J1459".
    the other immune globulin is furnished to Hal.
    claim 2 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the diagnosis code of Hal is "D80.0".
    the other immune globulin is an approved pooled plasma derivative for the treatment of primary immune deficiency disease.
    the other immune globulin is administered in the home.
    rn expects answers ["claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"] and unknowns ["the finding home administration appropriate about Hal is established"].
